      ":question/problem": "Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-3{x}^{2}+1$ defined on $[-3,3).$  Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-6x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-3{x}^{2}+1\u223c-8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{108(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-6x\u223c{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$"
