      ":question/problem": "Let $f(x)$ be the $8$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+4$ defined on $[-4,4).$  Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $8$-periodic extension of $G(x)=x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+4\u223c\\frac{20}{3}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is  \n{{field-2}}\nand  \n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\nx\u223c{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$"
